I think that any intellegent & tame monster should be able to act as
henchman.  (You could get a human henchman by finding a ghost, and
zaping the corpse with a wand of undead turning.)

I don't see any big deal about having the henchman map out the dungeon
for you.  Maybe it would tell you what it's home level looks like.

I would like to see a wider variety of commands for dealing with
intellegent pets/henchmen.  You should be able to give them items (which
they will use), get items from them (maybe that intellegent lich
henchmen won't give you back your Stormbringer though), yell for help, 
ask them to follow you, or ask them to wonder off by themselves.

I do not think that intellegent pets/henchmen should help you rob a shop.

And (one last thing) a tamed Troll, should after being killed and
regenerating, still be tame.  

